/a-79189751?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Mao Zedong was perhaps the most influential, and certainly one of the most controversial, figures in 20th-century China. Even five decades after his death, the legacy of his era continues to influence China today.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Ratko Mladic’s funeral casts shadow over Bosnia and Herzegovina vote</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0aa7c796df2c10f901e4a0994a25764e4553314712cec144d528c37cb29987af</id><updated>2026-09-08T19:29:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T14:09:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ratko-mladic-s-funeral-casts-shadow-over-bosnia-and-herzegovina-vote/a-79189319--342fd5cbe6c7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ratko-mladic-s-funeral-casts-shadow-over-bosnia-and-herzegovina-vote/a-79189319?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Ratko Mladic’s funeral in Belgrade, attended by Serbian and Bosnian Serb leaders, has deepened regional tensions and could affect the upcoming election in Bosnia and Herzegovina.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Japan's empty temples seek new ways to survive</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9a9bc263b4e2a3ff905b0d794fd62a45b9fc724a8ef41386f83200851a0b1b7f</id><updated>2026-09-08T19:28:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T12:31:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/japan-s-empty-temples-seek-new-ways-to-survive/a-79157964--7eea677a26bf.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/japan-s-empty-temples-seek-new-ways-to-survive/a-79157964?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">With a declining population, shrinking congregations and growing economic pressures, temples are struggling to stay relevant. As more temples are sold or closed, is religion in decline in modern Japan?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>US-Canada tariff dispute weighs on cross-border ties</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2c4ce66833f2a230d6112775a8fe034eedb9242b3c663b33860b84593a013c69</id><updated>2026-09-08T19:28:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T10:09:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/us-canada-tariff-dispute-weighs-on-cross-border-ties/a-78815803--082b25646c1e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/us-canada-tariff-dispute-weighs-on-cross-border-ties/a-78815803?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As Canada's retaliatory tariffs take effect, Canadian and US car industries fear the trade war will hit them hard, while Canadians are cutting back on travel.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Kenya: Crackdown on foreign traders prompts xenophobia fears</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:34aefad9a9b99f082d5b6d7bc4dda2590738726a9c65fb970776774054a1dc04</id><updated>2026-09-08T19:28:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T09:14:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/kenya-crackdown-on-foreign-traders-prompts-xenophobia-fears/a-79143847--a8e571d0a365.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/kenya-crackdown-on-foreign-traders-prompts-xenophobia-fears/a-79143847?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Concerns about xenophobia are rising in Kenya after President William Ruto ordered a crackdown on foreigners working as hawkers. The government insists however that legally documented foreign traders remain protected.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Morocco earthquake 3 years on: 'No one has remembered us'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2cd5d0eb1d16dd6a61a0422bba2fbed8ac033d522d88f0d9092dcb5bdca62054</id><updated>2026-09-08T19:29:58Z</updated><published>2026-09-07T18:57:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/morocco-earthquake-3-years-on-no-one-has-remembered-us/a-78874844--cbd4f3eb032b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/morocco-earthquake-3-years-on-no-one-has-remembered-us/a-78874844?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Morocco has rebuilt thousands of homes since the 2023 earthquake. But some survivors are still living in tents and say they have received no state aid.</summary><category term="Africa" /></entry><entry><title>Nicaragua challenges German arms exports to Israel at ICJ</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7ecf80da667eb3a8be4aad1ab557ee5513c47476f1b3df4d6a27501688f5cc3e</id><updated>2026-09-08T19:28:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-07T16:26:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/nicaragua-challenges-german-arms-exports-to-israel-at-icj/a-79148044--315737afbbdd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/nicaragua-challenges-german-arms-exports-to-israel-at-icj/a-79148044?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany has asked the International Court of Justice to dismiss the case on jurisdiction grounds. It also said its arms exports to Israel were documented, published, and subject to more stringent checks than most.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>War criminal Ratko Mladic buried with military honors in Belgrade, Serbia</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2cf4636c25c253204212c390cc4c842523c9872f27a70998fbac55a25ab2dcf5</id><updated>2026-09-08T19:28:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-07T15:03:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/war-criminal-ratko-mladic-buried-with-military-honors-in-belgrade-serbia/a-79148678--c4979d87a1d5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/war-criminal-ratko-mladic-buried-with-military-honors-in-belgrade-serbia/a-79148678?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Ratko Mladic, the former Bosnian Serb commander convicted of genocide in Srebrenica, has been buried in Belgrade. The funeral, broadcast live on TV, comes just days before President Vucic is expected to call an election.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Pakistan: Can creating new provinces fix governance?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3659f2782c5ad29c473a364f0f99b83eaa3c8a1d2f4f6ea0509007fc3cd41844</id><updated>2026-09-08T19:28:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-07T13:55:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/pakistan-can-creating-new-provinces-fix-governance/a-79148059--3974ef70363a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/pakistan-can-creating-new-provinces-fix-governance/a-79148059?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Pakistanis broadly agree that the country needs more responsive and effective government, but many question whether simply creating more provinces is the solution.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Threatening letters revive fears among Kashmiri Pandits</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7c1211b1dcb5a6f0a092ebe6d311ee00574bb0a82d42fe1080fa98e699b7d39c</id><updated>2026-09-08T19:28:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-07T12:41:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/threatening-letters-revive-fears-among-kashmiri-pandits/a-79144481--ac4e07371076.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/threatening-letters-revive-fears-among-kashmiri-pandits/a-79144481?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Leaked addresses and phone numbers have reignited fears among Hindu government employees who returned to Muslim-majority Kashmir under a rehabilitation scheme.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>US envoys Witkoff and Kushner hold Ukraine talks after meeting Putin</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:64b9cb1112024ae2953cdd27f6bf5c3cf7e46861ad850edba3b9f867d6d7eee2</id><updated>2026-09-08T19:28:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-06T22:22:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/us-envoys-witkoff-and-kushner-hold-ukraine-talks-after-meeting-putin/a-79054779--687b66a14041.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/us-envoys-witkoff-and-kushner-hold-ukraine-talks-after-meeting-putin/a-79054779?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">US envoys Steve Witkoff and Jared Kushner held talks with Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelenskyy in Kyiv, seeking to revive efforts to end the war. But the latest diplomatic push seems to have produced no breakthrough.</summary><category term="News" /></entry></feed>
